// Quiz for DELETE topic

::DELETE::
How does DELETE differ from TRUNCATE? {
~DELETE removes the entire table from the database, TRUNCATE maintains the table structure.
=DELETE removes each record one at a time logging every deletion, making it slower than TRUNCATE.
~DELETE removes by deallocating the data pages used to store the records, making it faster that TRUNCATE
~DELETE and TRUNCATE do the same exact thing, TRUNCATE is just more efficient.
}

